// The spec heading shape, gated by MD043 required-headings.
//
// MD043 takes one `headings` array, so each fixed shape needs its own config
// file and its own hook entry. `?` matches exactly one heading and stands in
// for the varying title; `+` matches one or more and so fails a spec with no
// requirement in it. MD043 checks every level, which is why the requirement
// and scenario headings are covered by that trailing `+` rather than ignored.
//
// Precondition: the project's general `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc` must not
// mention MD043 at any value, including false. It merges over this file and
// would disable the shape while the hook kept reporting success.
{
  "config": {
    "MD043": {
      "headings": [
        "?",
        "## Purpose",
        "## Requirements",
        "+"
      ]
    }
  }
}
